.TH USB-SSH 1 "2026-07-16" "gway-001" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-ssh \- SSH through the bastion USB unlock key workflow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-ssh
.RI [ --workgroup " NAME" ]
.I command
.br
.B usb-ssh
.RI [ --workgroup " NAME" ]
.RI [ ssh-args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-ssh
wraps SSH access behind a local bastion USB unlock workflow. Without a named
command, it behaves like
.BR ssh (1)
after decrypting the bastion key from the inserted unlock USB into a temporary
local key for that connection.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI register " user@host"
Show manual remote registration steps for the current bastion public key, then
test key-based access after registration is completed.
.TP
.B status
Show bastion USB state, optional bastion agent cache state, and active
usb-ssh client sessions.
.TP
.B sessions
Show active usb-ssh client sessions only.
.TP
.B unlock
Mount the original unlock USB and refresh the optional bastion agent cache.
.TP
.B lock
Clear the optional bastion agent cache and release the fixed unlock mount.
.TP
.B refresh
Refresh the optional bastion agent cache once.
.TP
.B copy
Copy the current bastion USB unlock folder to another USB key.
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --workgroup " NAME"
Record the workgroup identity in
.IR /home/arthe/logs/usb-interactions.log .
.SH EXAMPLES
Show bastion USB status:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/usb-ssh status
.fi
.PP
Unlock and refresh the local agent cache:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/usb-ssh --workgroup FieldOps unlock
.fi
.PP
Use the wrapper as SSH:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/usb-ssh ubuntu@arthexis.com
.fi
.PP
Register a new remote account:
.PP
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/usb-ssh register ubuntu@example.com
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /mnt/bastion-unlock/bastion-ssh
Fixed unlock mount location.
.TP
.I /run/bastion-ssh/agent.sock
Optional bastion agent socket.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/logs/usb-interactions.log
Workgroup-tagged interaction log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR remote-up (1)
